                <th class="p-4">Clinical Inclusions</th>
                <th class="p-4">Published Fee (INR)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-japandi-clay/20">
              <tr>
                <td class="p-4 font-medium text-japandi-charcoal">New Patient Consultation (Incl. RVG X-ray)</td>
                <td class="p-4">Clinical periodontal examination &amp; digital radiograph</td>
                <td class="p-4 text-japandi-moss font-semibold">₹600</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-4 font-medium text-japandi-charcoal">Deep Periodontal Scaling / Root Planing</td>
                <td class="p-4">Subgingival ultrasonic debridement, root planing &amp; antiseptic irrigation</td>
                <td class="p-4 text-japandi-moss font-semibold">₹8,000 – ₹15,000</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Symptoms & When to Seek Periodontal Care -->
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">
          When Should You Consult a Dentist for Gum Care?
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          Gum disease is often silent in its earliest stages, which is why many patients do not seek treatment until significant bone support is compromised. We recommend booking an evaluation if you notice:
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 text-xs sm:text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light">
          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2.5">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">Common Symptoms</h4>
            <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc list-inside">
              <li>Pink toothbrush bristles or blood spitting when brushing.</li>
              <li>Puffy, tender, or purplish-red gums.</li>
              <li>Chronic unpleasant breath or bad taste in the mouth.</li>
              <li>Receding gum margins making teeth look abnormally long.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2.5">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">Advanced Warning Signs</h4>
            <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc list-inside">
              <li>Pus discharge or small pockets between teeth and gums.</li>
              <li>Slight loosening or mobility in permanent adult teeth.</li>
              <li>Shifting spaces or newly developing gaps between teeth.</li>
              <li>Changes in how your upper and lower teeth meet during chewing.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Transit & Accessibility -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">
          Visiting Aureva Dental for Gum Treatment in Hennur
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          Located on the 2nd Floor of SLV Nilaya on Horamavu Agara Road (beside Nayara Petrol Bunk), Aureva Dental is conveniently accessible for residents across North-East Bangalore:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-xs sm:text-sm text-japandi-earth space-y-1.5 font-light">
          <li><strong>Hennur Bande &amp; Horamavu Agara Road:</strong> Less than 2 minutes away.</li>
          <li><strong>Hennur Main Road &amp; Geddalahalli:</strong> 5 minutes via Hennur Bande Road.</li>
          <li><strong>Horamavu, Babusapalya &amp; Kalkere:</strong> 6 to 8 minutes.</li>
          <li><strong>Kalyan Nagar, HRBR Layout &amp; Kammanahalli:</strong> 10 minutes via Hennur Cross.</li>
